load\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review refreshed for Option B residual live reconcile-check retirement in fresh worktree retire-reconcile-check; beginning held-out TDD and implementation. Root-cause hypothesis: prior child work removed the user-facing mode flag but left the engine cap-0 sentinel, CI compatibility choices, bridge-runner mapping, and schema prose using the retired vocabulary.","timestamp":1788635580199384001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"STOPPED per leaf protocol: updated plan-review for the actual Option B edit set still BLOCKs. Blocking RCA: retiring Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK while obeying the operator carve-out to leave _ref_lock.py:658/717 unchanged breaks the bridge pause/phase gate, because the retained pause writer still emits gated_mode=\"reconcile-check\" and _advisory_lock resolves that value through Mode.from_str. Without changing that state writer/decoder contract to a non-reconcile spelling (or adding another live alias containing the retired vocabulary), the rollout-safety pause behavior cannot be preserved and AC2 cannot be literally satisfied. No --force used; no Gerrit push/close attempted.","timestamp":1788640052309333001}],"created_at":1788314329437517001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f9fd1e1e-3e8c-46a0-b747-33aa9371c388","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"f1a4-1b43-b720-4dab"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe legacy `reconcile` family spans CLI registration, direct-engine modes, library/MCP `mode=` acceptance, compatibility profiles, exit behavior, manifests/tallies, and `bridge_state/reconcile-check.json`. It is not a simple rename. In particular, historical `\"reconcile-check\"` state appears in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py:658,717`.\n\n## Approach\n\nThis container separates canonical bridge capability migration from deletion of legacy command/mode/state surfaces. Child 1 maps and implements all useful reconcile-check observables under `bridge preview`, `bridge fsck`, `bridge status`, or one coherent new bridge diagnostic subverb. Child 2 removes CLI/direct-engine modes and persisted-state compatibility only after migration. Child 3 removes library/MCP compatibility methods and schemas after the new bridge contracts are live.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Canonical bridge operations retain or explicitly retire every current reconcile-check observable with documented evidence.\n- [ ] No live route, mode, state path, docs, schema, or compatibility profile retains `reconcile` or `reconcile-check` vocabulary.\n- [ ] Persisted historical reconcile-check data is migrated or read by a narrowly retained decoder until safe to retire.\n- [ ] CLI, Python, and MCP consumers use explicit bridge operations rather than compatibility `mode=` dispatch.\n\n## Final AC2 Option B execution note\n\nThe human operator selected Option B for this final in-scope completion pass: retire the residual live `reconcile-check` vocabulary from the reconciler mode taxonomy, bridge-runner compatibility profile, GitHub Actions/Jenkins provider mode choices, live schema prose, live operator docs, and affected tests while preserving the read-only discrepancy capability through `bridge preview` / `dry-run` routing.\n\nAC3 carve-out and decoder refinement: the operator explicitly directed this pass not to edit `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py` at the pause-state decoder/writer lines around 658/717. Because that carved-out writer still persists the historical pause sentinel `gated_mode=\"reconcile-check\"`, this pass keeps a narrow `Mode.from_str()` decode alias that maps only that persisted sentinel to the live cap-0 `DRY_RUN` floor. The alias is not a selectable enum member, is not listed in `MODE_CAPS` or allowed-mode errors, and exists only so AC3 historical pause data keeps blocking write-capable modes (`bootstrap-strict`, `bootstrap-throttle`, `live`) while live route/profile/mode/docs/schema vocabulary is retired.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","reason":"Keep CI provider bridge mode choices coherent after retiring reconcile-check compatibility profile."},{"path":"Jenkinsfile","reason":"Keep CI provider bridge mode choices coherent after retiring reconcile-check compatibility profile."},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"Remove live operator documentation that advertised retained reconcile-check compatibility vocabulary."},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"Remove live operator documentation that advertised retained reconcile-check compatibility vocabulary."},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"Remove live operator documentation that advertised retained reconcile-check compatibility vocabulary."},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"Remove live operator documentation that advertised retained reconcile-check compatibility vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py","reason":"Remove reconcile-check compatibility profile mapping; dry-run remains the preview profile."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_preflight.py","reason":"Update live reconciler consumer prose/logic after retiring reconcile-check mode vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_recovery.py","reason":"Update live reconciler consumer prose/logic after retiring reconcile-check mode vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_walk.py","reason":"Update live reconciler consumer prose/logic after retiring reconcile-check mode vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"Update live reconciler consumer prose/logic after retiring reconcile-check mode vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/get_rotation.py","reason":"Update live reconciler consumer prose/logic after retiring reconcile-check mode vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/load_phase.py","reason":"Update live reconciler consumer prose/logic after retiring reconcile-check mode vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mode.py","reason":"Retire reconcile-check enum/cap entry while retaining the AC3 narrow decode alias to DRY_RUN for persisted pause sentinels."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/pass_support.py","reason":"Update live reconciler consumer prose/logic after retiring reconcile-check mode vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"Update live reconciler consumer prose/logic after retiring reconcile-check mode vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py","reason":"Keep direct --mode reconcile-check rejected before operational work while the persisted-state decoder remains internal-only."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/ticket_planner.py","reason":"Update live reconciler consumer prose/logic after retiring reconcile-check mode vocabulary."},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json","reason":"Reword live schema descriptions to avoid retired vocabulary."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_filter_local_ids_engine_restore_82bb_heldout.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconcile_cli_state_removal_82bb_heldout.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_recovery_write_boundary.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_ticket_plan_shadow.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_internal_shim_removal.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_primary_workflow_heldout.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py","reason":"Update tests/held-out oracles to assert residual live vocabulary retirement, direct CLI rejection, and preserved pause protection for write-capable modes."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","f1a4-1b43-b720-4dab"],["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"ab51c092-c4e4-41ad-802c-d6d51dae0ed6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","reconciler","breaking-change","compatibility"],"ticket_id":"0cfc-e511-8f8a-4c8b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Retire the reconcile and reconcile-check compatibility family","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cd073a66-bba0-42de-ad1a-286e5c29d7dc","ab51c092-c4e4-41ad-802c-d6d51dae0ed6","e15ead43-0fc4-4849-b053-a846279dfd77","1cca5429-7c2c-4f19-8258-05c938bec241","4c3e4045-1822-40a5-81d4-d52227ed6a11","ab4bf8b7-50a1-4e30-9dab-8710d59990b5","0089c802-6250-4566-8a76-62d5123619f8","b0757905-c680-47b2-bfc8-7bfc68a28203","6e42b622-0982-49fa-9541-e5c3f9ce8f1f","f437d5f0-0e8d-4bac-9611-1583a0a52e25","1fd06de6-5ccc-4c16-8bac-ec8475759a2a","8e95ce29-7583-4ed1-a314-e75577b2bc13","e16db7db-de21-425d-bb52-9ecda161a1ac","1a1494e1-540b-4e72-a5bd-641aed747de8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"